C-73: mediate PowerShell, and record the size of the unrecognised surface

The Bash path is the most defended surface in this project: structural
tokenisation, allowlist, denylist, interpreter hardening, and nine fail-opens
closed in one day, guarded by fifty proofs. Beside it sat a PowerShell tool
with the same capability on the same machine, and the membrane did not know it
existed. A live call produced no audit entry at all — not ALLOW, not DENY, not
even PASSTHROUGH — because the installer writes an enumerated matcher and that
name was not on it.

Every shell protection built today was one tool name away from irrelevant.

Both shells now map to SHELL/exec and reach identical verdicts, and the
installer's matcher names PowerShell. Reproduced before fixing: `git push` and
`wget` were refused under Bash and allowed under PowerShell.

Two things this is NOT.

It is not comprehension of PowerShell. core/shell_policy.py tokenises
POSIX-style, and PowerShell is not POSIX — its backtick escapes rather than
substitutes. The mismatch runs towards over-blocking, which is the safe
direction, but the boundary on this host stays the filesystem write-scope and
the network out-scope, as C-63 already says for interpreters in general.

It is not the fix for the underlying defect. Adding names to a set is the
enumeration this project keeps having to undo — the same shape as the separator
list, the anchor list and the environment-variable list. It closes the one gap
that was measured to be severe. O-33 stays open.

THE SURFACE, MEASURED.

The audit's entire history — 7652 entries — was produced by exactly five tool
names: Bash 1795, Edit 1351, Write 390, Read 146, WebFetch 32, plus three
PASSTHROUGH names from Cursor. Two of the seven names in the matcher,
MultiEdit and NotebookEdit, have never appeared at all.

Against that, the tool inventory reachable in one live session is about 73
names (14 direct, 23 deferred, 6 auth, 30 MCP). The matcher routes roughly one
name in ten. Confirmed live: Glob, Grep and PowerShell calls leave no trace of
any kind.

Effect-capable examples that remain unmediated: Artifact (publishes content to
the web), 27 mcp__alpaca__* tools (network and account data), WebSearch,
Glob/Grep/LSP (filesystem read), EnterWorktree/ExitWorktree (filesystem writes
via git), Agent/Skill, and SendMessage/PushNotification/RemoteTrigger/Cron*
(external or scheduled effects).

The number worth remembering is not ten percent. It is that the project cannot
say what the other sixty-six names do, which is the definition of an unmeasured
attack surface.

Suite: 52 proofs, 51 pass + 1 skip. Ledger: 52 proven, 6 blocked, 4 planned of
73; 18 open obstacles of 34.

